@startuml receipt-archive-states
title M-UM3: receipt evidence and retirement fate (v0 design; no implementation claim)
hide empty description

state "Start receipt / execution evidence (§§4.7, 7)" as Receipt {
  state "No start receipt yet" as NoReceipt
  state "Root start receipt exists\nwritten before privilege drop / exec" as Recorded
  state "Process absence confirmed ONLY\nresult receipt: remaining = 0" as Absent
  [*] --> NoReceipt
  NoReceipt --> Recorded : launcher: setsid, atomic root write\nthen clear groups / GID / UID / exec
  Recorded --> Recorded : launch with existing execution_id refuses\nexecution_already_started
  Recorded --> Recorded : helper stop refuses receipt / live identity mismatch\nor processes_remain / unknown observation
  Recorded --> Absent : helper exec.stop verifies active owned generation,\nreceipt + live identity; TERM / grace / KILL;\nno remaining processes incl. escaped descendants
  Absent --> Absent : effect/receipt evidence retained for reconciliation\nno second-launch permission inferred
}
note right of Recorded
  Process: swarma-user-launcher, root until UID drop.
  Root-owned mode 0644 start receipt:
  execution_id, epoch, pid, start_time, boot_id, session_id.
  Location binds generation and execution_id (§7).
  Process: swarma-user-manager, root, owns exec.stop.
  Execution: curator-run -> harness under agent UID;
  dispatcher service UID owns execution lifetime.
  Unknown/failed observation is not known absence (§4.7).
  Post-receipt/pre-exec failure resolves same effect/receipt; never launch twice.
  Evidence retained until original identities permanently inadmissible (§4.6).
  Exact retention bounds / coverage rule open (§14 question 8).
  R-FD3: generation lock through root receipt and verified UID/GID drop;
  verified executable handle through exec; executor only 0-2 and read-only FD3.
end note
note right of Absent
  Evidence condition, not a new persisted account state.
  No harness native-lock absence attested by exec.stop (§4.7).
  Host recovery: fresh runner under agent UID checks native lock
  under closed fence; unknown result keeps session parked (session-host §3.5).
  Stop/effect evidence retention governed by §4.6; concrete encoding/bounds open (§14 question 8).
  An existing start receipt still refuses another start (§7).
end note

state "Home fate after retiring commit and verified quiescence (§4.4.1)" as Retirement {
  state "Home in quarantine\nsame-filesystem move; root-controlled" as Quarantined
  state "Declared keys destroyed\nbefore deletion walk" as KeysDestroyed
  state "Home deleted\nno agent content retained" as Deleted
  [*] --> Quarantined : manager user.retire; account quiescent
  Quarantined --> Quarantined : key destruction failed/unknown\nno walk; remain retiring; audit
  Quarantined --> KeysDestroyed : destroy declared keys; journal under shared lock\nrecovery confirms destruction or prior absence
  KeysDestroyed --> KeysDestroyed : deletion failed/partial/unknown\nremain retiring; audit; unreadable is not absent
  KeysDestroyed --> Deleted : no-follow descriptor deletion\nunlink all home content/names/links
}
note right of Quarantined
  swarma-user-manager, root; caller roles apply (§3).
  Dispatcher only its own agents; quarantine root 0700 (§4.0).
  Journal recovery resumes retirement forward (§4.6).
  Labels illustrate sequence, not new persisted ledger states.
  Declared paths and audit encoding unpublished (§14 question 6).
  No arbitrary-home secret classifier; no archive/delete/keep selector.
  Separate explicit operator home retention: confidentiality not guaranteed;
  format/ordering unpublished (§14 question 1), not admitted by user.retire.
end note

state "Metadata export only (schema publication gate, §4.4.1)" as Metadata {
  state "Closed-schema service-generated export\nroot-owned 0600 in root 0700 archive directory" as Exported
  state "Metadata swept" as Swept
  [*] --> Exported : schema/provenance published and qualified;\ntrusted service records only
  Exported --> Swept : archive.sweep: older than max_age\nthen oldest until max_total satisfied
}
note right of Exported
  No agent-controlled strings, names, links or bodies; no home source.
  Unknown provenance/schema failure prevents publication.
  Schema/naming/bounds/audit encoding unpublished (§14 question 6).
  Code/results/git/free-text logs have separate confidentiality policy.
  Sweep only metadata, never live effect/receipt/removal evidence (§4.6).
  Sweep at every retirement and daily root timer; timer details/retry unpublished.
end note

note "R-OBS (§§2, 4.5-4.6): original principal/operator observes under journal lock.\nExactly recorded (result + current state), pending, rolled_back, not_recorded, unavailable, contradictory.\nComplete authoritative evidence required for not_recorded; expired/missing/unreadable evidence = unavailable.\nObservation never authorises a new effect; concrete retention/coverage publication remains open (§14 question 8)." as Observation
Observation .. Receipt

note "Defining spec: [[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher §7 start receipt]],\n[[../spec/helper.md#47-execstop §4.7 stop evidence]], [[../spec/helper.md#441-retirement-deletion-and-metadata-export §4.4.1 deletion/export]].\nThese are independent evidence, deletion and export views, not a receipt-to-export transition.\nCurrent repository: nothing implemented. v1 retains egress until account/group removal (§8).\nv2 grant grammar open (§9); SH2+ joint admission remains I4-gated (§§7, 14).\nOnly the dispatcher invokes the launcher; FD3 platform mechanism open (§14 question 7)." as Scope
Scope .. Receipt
Scope .. Retirement
Scope .. Metadata
@enduml
